This is the sole content source for the dns-network-ops umbrella. All umbrella body and
reference material derives from skills/networking/dns/. MIT licence governs the umbrella
SKILL.md and all four references.

Files folded -> reference mapping:
  skills/networking/dns/SKILL.md
    -> SKILL.md (umbrella body: authoritative vs recursive classification, platform selection,
       reference router, vendor-skill routing table, cross-refs, red flags, bottom line)
    -> references/platform-architecture.md (cross-platform feature matrix, platform comparison,
       architecture patterns, DNS security layers by platform, platform routing summary)
  skills/networking/dns/references/concepts.md
    -> references/concepts.md (resolution flow, record types, zone transfers AXFR/IXFR/NOTIFY/TSIG,
       caching and TTL strategy, negative caching, split-horizon implementation)
    -> references/dnssec.md (chain of trust, KSK/ZSK/CSK key types, DS records, validation process,
       algorithm recommendations, NSEC vs NSEC3, plus an added rollover-failure-modes section)
    -> references/dns-security-and-encryption.md (DoH/DoT/DoQ comparison, RPZ triggers and actions,
       DNS sinkholing, cloud DNS firewall, response rate limiting)

